issue:
reconnecting a derived leaks duplicate subscriptions

### Describe the bug

on Svelte 5.57.1, a previously evaluated, disconnected derived can subscribe twice to a newly discovered dependency when a tracked reader attaches. disposing the reader and owner removes only one subscription, leaving the disposed graph retained by the source.

this reproduces in both development and production. the repro uses internal signal APIs to make the duplicate registration observable without relying on garbage-collection timing.


### Reproduction

in an empty project, install the unpatched release:

```sh
npm add svelte@5.57.1
```

`repro.mjs`:

```js
import { source, set } from './node_modules/svelte/src/internal/client/reactivity/sources.js';
import { derived } from './node_modules/svelte/src/internal/client/reactivity/deriveds.js';
import { effect_root, render_effect } from './node_modules/svelte/src/internal/client/reactivity/effects.js';
import { get, untrack } from './node_modules/svelte/src/internal/client/runtime.js';
import { flushSync } from './node_modules/svelte/src/internal/client/reactivity/batch.js';

const enabled = source(false);
const shared = source(1);
let value;

const destroyOwner = effect_root(() => {
  value = derived(() => get(enabled) ? get(shared) : 0);
  untrack(() => get(value));
});

flushSync(() => set(enabled, true));
const destroyReader = effect_root(() => render_effect(() => get(value)));

console.log('subscriptions:', shared.reactions?.length ?? 0);
console.log('same reaction:', shared.reactions?.[0] === shared.reactions?.[1]);

destroyReader();
destroyOwner();
console.log('after disposal:', shared.reactions?.length ?? 0);
```

run with `node repro.mjs` or `NODE_ENV=production node repro.mjs`.

expected: one subscription while mounted, zero after disposal.

actual:

```text
subscriptions: 2
same reaction: true
after disposal: 1
```


